ation patterns, and the results indicate that VHL gene mutation is associated exclusively with the development of non-papillary tumours.\n\nNow I'm working out the exact character offsets for each entity annotation—mapping disease mentions like \"non-papillary renal cell carcinomas,\" \"sporadic renal cell carcinomas,\" \"parenchymal tumours of the kidney,\" and \"chromophobe renal cell carcinomas\" to their precise start and end positions, converting from relative to absolute coordinates using the offset of 112.\n\nI'm double-checking letter counts in several key phrases to verify my offset math is correct before finalizing, then classifying each mention as either DiseaseClass or SpecificDisease based on whether it refers to a broad category or a distinct entity. Once I've verified the spans, I'll assemble everything into a single JSON object with annotations, rationales, and guideline references for each disease mention.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "{\"annotations\":[{\"start\":75,\"end\":110,\"text\":\"non-papillary renal cell carcinomas\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"Non-papillary renal cell carcinomas refers to a family of multiple RCC subtypes rather than one specific disease, so it is a Disease Class.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1: Specific Disease and Disease Class\"},{\"start\":178,\"end\":208,\"text\":\"sporadic renal cell carcinomas\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"Sporadic renal cell carcinomas denotes a broad category of non-hereditary RCC that groups multiple specific diseases, so it is a Disease Class. The minimum span includes the qualifier sporadic.\",\"guideline_section\":\"What to Annotate 1: Specific Disease and Disease Class; What to Annotate 5: Minimum necessary span\"},{\"start\":224,\"end\":257,\"text\":\"parenchymal tumours of the kidney\",\"entity\":\"DiseaseClass\",\"rationale\":\"Refers to a family of kidney tumours that encompasses several specific diseases (e.g., RCC subtypes, oncocytom